{"step_index":32,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T15:51:49Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-24T21:21:49+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-24T21:21:50+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.txt`\nTotal Lines: 229\nTotal Bytes: 7888\nShowing lines 1 to 50\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ================================================================================\n2: HALF-YEARLY EXAMINATION 2026-27\n3: CLASS XII - MATHEMATICS (SET A)\n4: Time Allowed: 3 Hours                                          Maximum Marks: 80\n5: ================================================================================\n6: \n7: GENERAL INSTRUCTIONS:\n8: 1. This question paper contains 38 questions. All questions are compulsory.\n9: 2. This question paper is divided into FIVE Sections - Section A, B, C, D and E.\n10: 3. In Section A - Questions no. 1 to 18 are Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs) and questions no. 19 and 20 are Assertion-Reason based questions of 1 mark each.\n11: 4. In Section B - Questions no. 21 to 25 are Very Short Answer (VSA) type questions, carrying 2 marks each.\n12: 5. In Section C - Questions no. 26 to 31 are Short Answer (SA) type questions, carrying 3 marks each.\n13: 6. In Section D - Questions no. 32 to 35 are Long Answer (LA) type questions, carrying 5 marks each.\n14: 7. In Section E - Questions no. 36 to 38 are Case-Based integrated units of assessment carrying 4 marks each with sub-parts of values 2, 1 and 1 mark each respectively.\n15: 8. There is no overall choice. However, an internal choice has been provided in some questions.\n16: 9. Use of calculators is not permitted.\n17: \n18: ================================================================================\n19: SECTION A\n20: (Questions 1 to 20 carry 1 mark each)\n21: ================================================================================\n22: \n23: Q1. Let A = {1, 2, 3} and R = {(1, 1), (2, 2), (3, 3), (1, 2)} be a relation on A. Then R is:\n24: (a) An equivalence relation\n25: (b) Reflexive and transitive only\n26: (c) Reflexive and symmetric only\n27: (d) Symmetric and transitive only\n28: \n29: Q2. The function f : ℝ → ℝ defined by f(x) = x² is:\n30: (a) One-one and onto\n31: (b) One-one but not onto\n32: (c) Onto but not one-one\n33: (d) Neither one-one nor onto\n34: \n35: Q3. The principal value of sin⁻¹(-1/2) is:\n36: (a) π/6\n37: (b) -π/6\n38: (c) 5π/6\n39: (d) -5π/6\n40: \n41: Q4. The domain of cos⁻¹(2x - 1) is:\n42: (a) [0, 1]\n43: (b) [-1, 1]\n44: (c) [-1, 0]\n45: (d) [0, 2]\n46: \n47: Q5. For any square matrix A, the matrix (A + Aᵀ) is always:\n48: (a) Skew-symmetric\n49: (b) Symmetric\n50: (c) A diagonal matrix\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
