{"step_index":40,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T15:52:14Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-24T21:22:14+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-24T21:22:15+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt`\nTotal Lines: 729\nTotal Bytes: 27585\nShowing lines 680 to 729\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n680:       = 0.015(9) - 0.12 + 30\n681:       = 0.135 - 0.12 + 30\n682:       = 0.015 + 30 = ₹ 30.015                                            [1 mark]\n683: \n684: Final Answer: ₹ 30.015 (or 30.015)\n685: \n686: (iii) State, with reason, whether the cost is increasing or decreasing at x = 3 (1 mark):\n687: Since MC(3) = (dC/dx)|_{x=3} = 30.015 > 0,\n688: the rate of change of cost with respect to output is positive.\n689: Therefore, the cost is increasing at x = 3 units.                        [1 mark]\n690: \n691: Final Answer: Cost is increasing because dC/dx > 0 at x = 3.\n692: \n693: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n694: Q38. Case Study 3 - Integrals\n695: Given: Velocity v(t) = 3t² - 12t + 9 (in m/s), and initial displacement s(0) = 0.\n696: \n697: (i) Find the displacement function s(t) (2 marks):\n698: s(t) = ∫ v(t) dt = ∫ (3t² - 12t + 9) dt                                  [½ mark]\n699:      = 3(t³/3) - 12(t²/2) + 9t + C\n700:      = t³ - 6t² + 9t + C                                                 [1 mark]\n701: \n702: Given s(0) = 0:\n703: s(0) = 0³ - 6(0)² + 9(0) + C = 0 ⇒ C = 0                                 [½ mark]\n704: Therefore, s(t) = t³ - 6t² + 9t.\n705: \n706: Final Answer: s(t) = t³ - 6t² + 9t\n707: \n708: (ii) Find the displacement at t = 2 s (1 mark):\n709: s(2) = (2)³ - 6(2)² + 9(2)\n710:      = 8 - 6(4) + 18\n711:      = 8 - 24 + 18\n712:      = 2 m                                                               [1 mark]\n713: \n714: Final Answer: 2 m\n715: \n716: (iii) Find value(s) of t ∈ [0, 3] at which particle is momentarily at rest (1 mark):\n717: The particle is momentarily at rest when v(t) = 0.                       [½ mark]\n718: 3t² - 12t + 9 = 0\n719: 3(t² - 4t + 3) = 0\n720: 3(t - 1)(t - 3) = 0\n721: ⇒ t = 1 s or t = 3 s.\n722: Both t = 1 s and t = 3 s belong to [0, 3].                               [½ mark]\n723: \n724: Final Answer: t = 1 s and t = 3 s\n725: \n726: ================================================================================\n727: -- End of Marking Scheme --\n728: ================================================================================\n729: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
