 mark each)\n21: ================================================================================\n22: \n23: Q1. Let R = {(1,1), (2,2), (3,3), (1,3), (3,1)} be a relation on A = {1, 2, 3}. Then R is:\n24:     (a) Reflexive only\n25:     (b) Symmetric only\n26:     (c) An equivalence relation\n27:     (d) Reflexive and symmetric only\n28: \n29: Q2. The number of all one-one functions from the set {1, 2, 3} to itself is:\n30:     (a) 3\n31:     (b) 6\n32:     (c) 9\n33:     (d) 27\n34: \n35: Q3. The principal value of cos⁻¹(-1/√2) is:\n36:     (a) π/4\n37:     (b) 3π/4\n38:     (c) -π/4\n39:     (d) 5π/4\n40: \n41: Q4. The range of the principal value branch of tan⁻¹x is:\n42:     (a) [-π/2, π/2]\n43:     (b) (-π/2, π/2)\n44:     (c) [0, π]\n45:     (d) (0, π)\n46: \n47: Q5. If A and B are square matrices of the same order, then (A + B)ᵀ equals:\n48:     (a) Aᵀ + Bᵀ\n49:     (b) Aᵀ - Bᵀ\n50:     (c) AᵀBᵀ\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
