inal revenue function, MR(x) = dR/dx.                       (2 marks)\n225:     (ii) Find the marginal revenue when x = 7 units.                             (1 mark)\n226:     (iii) State, with reason, whether the revenue is increasing or decreasing at x = 7.  (1 mark)\n227: \n228: Q38. Case Study - Integrals\n229:     A car starts from rest and its velocity at time t seconds is given by:\n230:     v(t) = 6t² - 4t (in m/s).\n231:     It is given that the displacement at t = 0 is zero, i.e. s(0) = 0.\n232:     Based on the above information, answer the following:\n233:     (i) Find the displacement function s(t).                                     (2 marks)\n234:     (ii) Find the displacement at t = 3 s.                                       (1 mark)\n235:     (iii) Find the value of t (t > 0) at which the car is momentarily at rest.   (1 mark)\n236: \n237: ================================================================================\n238:                            -- End of Question Paper --\n239: ================================================================================\n240: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
